        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Problem 3",
      "sourcePages": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You are given a grid of cells. Each cell has a positive integer written on it. You can move from a cell $x$ to a cell $y$ if $x$ and $y$ are in the same row or same column, and the number in $y$ is strictly smaller than the number in $x$. You want to colour some cells red so that:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Every cell can be reached by starting at a red cell and following a sequence of zero or more moves as defined above.",
            "The number of red cells is as small as possible."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You should report the following information:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "The number of red cells.",
            "The smallest number appearing amongst all red cells."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If there are multiple valid solutions, give any one solution."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For example, suppose the grid is as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": null,
          "rows": [
            [
              "2",
              "2",
              "3"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "1",
              "2"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "2",
              "2"
            ]
          ],
          "caption": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "It is sufficient to colour the two cells labelled 3, and one cannot do better than this. In this case, the number of red cells is 2 and the smallest number appearing amongst all red cells is 3."
        }
      ],
